1
00:00:05,209 --> 00:00:07,260
Hello, I'm Sangsoo Jeong.

2
00:00:07,714 --> 00:00:11,700
This time too, let's continue coloring this picture.

3
00:00:13,309 --> 00:00:18,400
Do you remember the clothing detail from when I sketched the prototype version?

4
00:00:18,401 --> 00:00:19,401
It's this part here.

5
00:00:20,790 --> 00:00:26,961
I didn't express it in the sketch of the current picture, because I wanted to draw it after confirming the clothing folds to some extent.

6
00:00:28,350 --> 00:00:32,880
Now that the fold areas are somewhat expressed, let me render that planned detail.

7
00:00:35,895 --> 00:00:40,521
Since it's a diamond shape, I'll draw a grid in a diamond pattern.

8
00:00:41,980 --> 00:00:46,830
Naturally, considering the folds.

9
00:00:46,831 --> 00:00:49,630
It'd be good to be accurate, but it's hard.

10
00:00:49,631 --> 00:00:52,910
I'm trying to draw it accurately too.

11
00:00:52,911 --> 00:00:54,430
It's not easy.

12
00:00:54,431 --> 00:00:56,590
I'm fudging it moderately.

13
00:01:33,664 --> 00:01:37,180
I don't like the left part, so I'm redrawing it.

14
00:01:37,180 --> 00:01:40,820
The grid size was smaller than the right side.

15
00:01:44,889 --> 00:01:47,260
This is truly boring labor.

16
00:01:47,261 --> 00:01:48,220
But what can you do?

17
00:01:48,269 --> 00:01:51,180
You can't only draw fun things.

18
00:01:51,181 --> 00:01:54,460
I've always done this detail work.

19
00:01:54,461 --> 00:02:01,660
It's so boring I could die, but once it's done I feel proud and the picture quality improves, so I can't give up.

20
00:02:04,889 --> 00:02:08,860
Since the folds are more wrinkled than the right side, it's hard.

21
00:02:08,861 --> 00:02:12,300
I'm at the point where I don't even know if I'm doing this right while drawing.

22
00:02:12,301 --> 00:02:13,020
Well, what can you do?

23
00:02:13,021 --> 00:02:14,860
I just express it within my ability.

24
00:02:15,900 --> 00:02:19,660
At times like this, I also want to learn 3D properly.

25
00:02:19,661 --> 00:02:23,301
I think it'd be convenient to pick it out in 3D and retouch it.

26
00:02:32,700 --> 00:02:38,140
Since I drew the big grid, let me draw the small grid inside.

27
00:02:38,141 --> 00:02:41,381
If you draw it finely from the start, it's hard to establish the form.

28
00:02:42,329 --> 00:02:46,140
Remember: draw big, then draw finely.

29
00:02:46,141 --> 00:02:47,180
That's such a good phrase.

30
00:02:47,181 --> 00:02:49,180
You can apply it anywhere.

31
00:02:53,950 --> 00:02:58,281
Let me separate the areas, as I did in the sketch.

32
00:03:03,739 --> 00:03:06,750
I'll use the straight-line lasso tool.

33
00:03:06,751 --> 00:03:10,590
I created a new layer, poured color, and masked it.

34
00:03:18,624 --> 00:03:22,581
I plan to make this masked part a semi-transparent material.

35
00:03:25,950 --> 00:03:29,481
I was happy that this boring work was almost over.

36
00:03:30,269 --> 00:03:33,961
Not being able to imagine some incident that was to come.

37
00:03:43,215 --> 00:03:50,241
After cutting out this masked part and moving it to a new layer, I adjusted the opacity to make it semi-transparent.

38
00:03:51,480 --> 00:03:54,570
You can see the leg line that was hidden too.

39
00:03:54,571 --> 00:03:59,770
Then, through a curve adjustment, I changed it to be a bit darker, so I changed the inherent value.

40
00:04:00,989 --> 00:04:02,400
Nothing special, right?

41
00:04:02,401 --> 00:04:04,320
This is how amazing Photoshop is, everyone.

42
00:04:11,000 --> 00:04:14,611
Now let me also render the panel part that I had hidden.

43
00:04:22,755 --> 00:04:26,830
I paint the highlight on the surface angles where a highlight would form.

44
00:04:28,805 --> 00:04:32,480
I also express the thickness.

45
00:04:32,481 --> 00:04:38,601
I should consider the reflected light, and if there's a need for a highlight on the edges, draw it too.

46
00:04:39,640 --> 00:04:44,890
This kind of light calculation would be accurate if done in 3D, I think.

47
00:04:46,330 --> 00:04:49,461
But I think there's also appeal that comes from the clumsiness.

48
00:06:47,835 --> 00:06:53,480
Because of the video filming, I had too many programs open, so it seems my computer broke down.

49
00:06:53,481 --> 00:06:54,840
Photoshop crashed.

50
00:06:56,120 --> 00:07:05,490
Since I normally use the auto-recovery save every ten minutes, I thought I'd lose at most ten minutes, and turned Photoshop back on.

51
00:07:06,495 --> 00:07:09,610
But there was no recovery save.

52
00:07:09,611 --> 00:07:10,611
It was despairing.

53
00:07:11,455 --> 00:07:15,171
It seems I probably messed with the settings while explaining the Photoshop features.

54
00:07:16,535 --> 00:07:23,161
I turned it on to see how far I'd drawn and saved, and the really annoying part had gone away.

55
00:07:25,425 --> 00:07:28,890
I put everything down, went and ate a piece of tiramisu.

56
00:07:28,891 --> 00:07:33,850
My mental state was shattered, and I wanted to just melt away, but I have to work according to schedule.

57
00:07:35,050 --> 00:07:37,450
It seems something like this happens every quarter.

58
00:07:37,451 --> 00:07:41,091
Always back up and save, two and three times over.

59
00:07:41,615 --> 00:07:47,290
Fortunately, there was the recorded video, so I used it to recover.

60
00:07:50,005 --> 00:07:54,910
Of all things, that had to go away, so I endured the urge to curse.

61
00:07:54,911 --> 00:07:56,110
Look, I held back.

62
00:07:56,219 --> 00:07:57,230
My mouth isn't moving.

63
00:08:00,950 --> 00:08:04,120
The occasionally moving mouth is a yawn.

64
00:08:04,121 --> 00:08:05,121
Yawn.

65
00:09:07,710 --> 00:09:11,310
After all the twists and turns, I completed the recovery.

66
00:09:11,311 --> 00:09:15,390
It seems my computer did that to create an episode for me.

67
00:09:15,390 --> 00:09:17,070
How impressive.

68
00:09:17,071 --> 00:09:18,830
Once I get paid, I should change my computer first.

69
00:09:20,890 --> 00:09:24,460
I'll wrap up this chapter here.

70
00:09:24,461 --> 00:09:27,781
Once you lose your work like this, the energy drains out of you.

71
00:09:29,345 --> 00:09:36,620
In the next chapter, I'll talk about and demo all sorts of methods to raise a picture's completion.

72
00:09:37,235 --> 00:09:40,140
You'll be seeing this picture again.

73
00:09:40,141 --> 00:09:41,141
Great work.
